BUG-12: System allows ordering more pieces than available stock while ordering the items.
    Issue Type:Bug
    Severity:Critical
    Priority:P1 (Highest)
    Test Data Used: Buyer: buyer1, Product: Chef's Basmati Rice (SKU-0007), Available Stock: 80 pieces, Case Size: 6 pieces, Ordered Qty: 15 cases (90 pieces), Created Order: WC-01008-1
      Summary: 
              As Per BR-01, stock is held in pieces, a case equals case_size pieces, and an order can never take more pieces than are in stock. When Chef's Basmati Rice had 80 pieces in stock, adding and checking out 15 cases (15 × 6 = 90 pieces) succeeded without any insufficient-stock error.
    Steps To Reproduce:
   1. Log in as buyer1 (Test@123) and open Chef's Basmati Rice (SKU-0007, stock: 80 pieces, Case of 6).
  2. Select unit Case, enter quantity 15 which is equal(15* 6=90)(90 pieces > 80 pieces), and click Add to cart.
  3. Go to Checkout, select a valid delivery date/slot, and click Place order.

    Expected Result:
Both Cart and Checkout must block 15 cases (90 pieces) because available stock is only 80 pieces .

  Actual Result:
The system allowed adding 15 cases to cart and created order WC-01008-1 for 90 pieces.


